# "Sacrifice a Treasure: Exile the top card of your library. You may play that card this turn." (CR 118.3, 601.3): the
# Treasure is the cost, so it leaves the battlefield as the ability is activated; the top card of Bot1's library (a
# Lightning Bolt) is exiled and Bot1 casts it from exile at Bot2 the same turn for 3 more damage (18 to 15). The red
# mana left over from the Mountain pays for it, so the sacrifice, not the mana, is what the Treasure bought.

